<title>JAPAN: Honda raises 96/97 group net forecast.</title>
<headline>Honda raises 96/97 group net forecast.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honda Motor Co Ltd said on Friday it expects its group net profit for the business year to March 31 to be about 220 billion yen, up from a November forecast of 200 billion yen.  </p>
<p>Honda, Japan's third-biggest carmaker, also expects group sales for 1996/97 to be above the November forecast of 5.10 trillion yen, a company spokesman said, without giving details.</p>
<p>The sales forecast was raised mainly due to the weaker yen, he said.</p>
</text>
